      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:9d1da28d69691765",
      "notice": null,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Mandarin for identifying number, then the Mandarin for to look for."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: 对不起",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "对不起 — duìbuqǐ — \"sorry\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "duìbuqǐ wǒ bù dǒng nǐ de huà — Sorry, I don't understand what you're saying."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The new character, in pieces: 起 (qǐ) — the walking piece read zǒu along the left and the bottom, carrying a three-stroke piece read jǐ, 'self', on its back: not the jǐ of 机. The next lesson puts it in your hand."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Its middle syllable loses its tone: duìbuqǐ, with bu light between two full syllables."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "对不起 (duìbuqǐ) is built from 对 'to answer, to match', 不 'not' and 起 (qǐ) 'to rise', all inherited from Middle Chinese, twojH, pjut and khiX (Guangyun, in Baxter's transcription). 'Not able to face you' is the usual explanation, but it is not settled."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for asking politely."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
